      "additional_risks": [
        {
          "detail": "The pod template changes spec.template.spec.containers[0].env[0].value and env[1].value, but both old and new values are redacted, so the diff cannot be verified. Trusted cases show fault-injection env values are drill-only: DEMO_STARTUP_FAIL=true causes new Pods to CrashLoop (release protection, not a healthy release), and DEMO_ERROR_RATE=1 makes real requests return 500. Require the rendered values to be the normal production values (e.g. DEMO_ERROR_RATE=0, no startup-fail flag) before merge.",
          "severity": "REVIEW",
          "title": "Redacted env value changes may ship drill fault settings"
        },
        {
          "detail": "KubeCPUOvercommit is firing and 35 scheduled Pods have no CPU/memory requests, so reported free capacity (2190m CPU) may be overstated. With maxUnavailable: 0 / maxSurge: 1 the rollout needs room for a surge Pod alongside the retained old Pod; verify capacity before syncing.",
          "severity": "REVIEW",
          "title": "Capacity headroom uncertain during rollout"
        },
        {
          "detail": "request_rate is 0 and error_ratio/p95 are null, so a successful rollout cannot be judged healthy from metrics alone; verify the new image digest and /version after sync.",
