      "status": "ok",
      "summary": "Release PR #9 replaces the demo Deployment image digest and bumps app.kubernetes.io/version labels on Deployment, Service, and ServiceMonitor, plus two redacted env values in the pod template. The decision preview is ERROR (AI_INVALID_RESULT), so this cannot be treated as approved. The two redacted env changes are the main unreviewed risk: trusted cases show that fault-injection env values (DEMO_STARTUP_FAIL=true, DEMO_ERROR_RATE=1) are drill-only and must not ship. Reviewers must confirm the env values are the normal production values before merge. Additional review items: KubeCPUOvercommit is firing and 35 scheduled Pods lack CPU/memory requests, so free capacity may be overstated; request_rate is 0, so zero errors/latency are not evidence of health. If a rollback is needed, it must be a Git revert commit plus Argo sync, not argocd app rollback or kubectl rollout undo."
